---
config:
  flowchart:
    nodeSpacing: 24
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: What the check of the translations finds
    accDescr: scripts/check-l10n.mjs reads the texts that the code translates, translate() and translatePlural() in js, ->t() and ->n() in templates and lib, and the texts that lib translates later, of a ConnectionCheck, an InvalidSettingException and the errors that a run keeps, with the constants that they name. It compares them with every catalog l10n/LANGUAGE.json. A text that a catalog lacks, a translation with other placeholders than its English one or with a lone percent sign, or a plural with other forms than the rule of its language fails the check with its place; it needs words. A text that no code translates, a text twice, or an l10n/LANGUAGE.js that differs from its l10n/LANGUAGE.json fails as well, and node scripts/check-l10n.mjs --fix drops the text and writes l10n/LANGUAGE.js anew. Otherwise the check passes.

    code["The code<br>js · templates · lib"]
    texts["`The texts it translates<br>*and those that lib*<br>*translates later*`"]
    catalog["Each catalog<br>l10n/LANGUAGE.json"]
    compare{"Each text once in each catalog,<br>with its placeholders and plural forms,<br>and nothing more?"}
    missing["❌ A missing text, other<br>placeholders or plural forms:<br>add the words"]
    unused["🔧 An unused text, one twice<br>or another l10n/LANGUAGE.js:<br>--fix drops it and writes it"]
    passed["✅ Passes: every text<br>is in every language"]

    code --> texts --> compare
    catalog --> compare
    compare -- "missing" --> missing
    compare -- "more" --> unused
    compare -- "yes" --> passed

    classDef source fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef check fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    classDef refused fill:#c9302c1f,stroke:#c9302c,stroke-width:2px
    class code,catalog source
    class texts,compare,unused check
    class passed done
    class missing refused
